UID:40af85a4-50c7-58dd-968a-ff8f81cde2ab
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T113000
DESCRIPTION:This presentation will provide an overview of understanding psy
 choeducational evaluation reports.  It will include a review of areas co
 mmonly assessed in school evaluations such as intellectual functioning\, p
 sychological processing\, adaptive behavior\, and social/emotional develo
 pment.  The presentation will focus on how toidentify your child’s stre
 ngths and weaknesses so that you understand their needs within the classro
 om setting\, as well as how to support them at home. This session is high
 ly recommended for families of students at all levels (elementary\, middl
 e\, and high school).     
LOCATION:437 Old Peachtree Road\, NW\, Suwanee\, GA   30024\, Building 200
 \, Central Gwinnett Room 2.111
SUMMARY:Parent Mentor Presents “Understanding Your Child as a Student”
END:VEVENT
